      "api_error_status": null,
      "result": "`api.customer_label` now formats names the same way the web view does, and it still returns `{\"label\": ...}`.\n\n**Change:** I edited only `api.py`. It now calls `labels.display_name`, the same function the web view (`web.customer_heading`) uses, instead of returning the raw name. That function collapses runs of whitespace into single spaces, trims both ends, and uses `\"Anonymous\"` when the name is empty or only whitespace.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m unittest test_sample` passes (1 test).\n- I compared `customer_label(n)` with `{\"label\": customer_heading(n)}` for `'Lee'`, `'  Ada   Lovelace '`, `''`, `'   '` and `'\\tBo\\nKim'`. They matched every time, giving `Lee`, `Ada Lovelace`, `Anonymous`, `Anonymous` and `Bo Kim`.\n- I deleted the `__pycache__/` folder the check created, so `api.py` is the only file that differs from before.\n\n**Limitation:** passing `None` or anything that isn't a string will raise an error, the same as in the web view. The request didn't say how to handle that, so I left it alone.",
